# SELinux file contexts for OPPO CPH1909 (A5s, MT6765)
#
# Minimal bring-up policy. The stock ColorOS policy declares ~200 MediaTek and
# OPPO specific types (mtk_hal_*, oppo_*) that do not exist in Android 10's
# sepolicy, so it cannot be reused directly. Rather than port all of it up
# front, this labels the vendor binaries against AOSP's standard hal_* types
# where a direct equivalent exists, and leaves the remainder to be added from
# real denials observed on device.
#
# NOTE: BOARD_SEPOLICY_DIRS pulls this in; the device also builds permissive
# during bring-up (see sepolicy/vendor/*.te) so that a missing rule logs
# instead of blocking boot.

###
### HAL services -- mapped to AOSP types
###
# Only services AOSP's own system/sepolicy/vendor/file_contexts does NOT already
# label are listed here. checkfc rejects a path regex that appears twice across
# the m4'd inputs ("Multiple same specifications"), even when both entries give
# the identical context, so eight upstream-identical lines were removed from this
# section: drm@1.0-service, gatekeeper@1.0-service,
# graphics.allocator@2.0-service, keymaster@3.0-service, media.omx@1.0-service,
# memtrack@1.0-service, vibrator@1.0-service and wifi@1.0-service. Their
# labelling is unchanged -- it just comes from AOSP now.
#
# The -mediatek / -service.widevine suffixed paths below are distinct regexes
# that upstream has no entry for, so they stay.
/(vendor|system/vendor)/bin/hw/android\.hardware\.audio@2\.0-service-mediatek                 u:object_r:hal_audio_default_exec:s0
/(vendor|system/vendor)/bin/hw/android\.hardware\.bluetooth@1\.0-service-mediatek             u:object_r:hal_bluetooth_default_exec:s0
/(vendor|system/vendor)/bin/hw/android\.hardware\.cas@1\.0-service                            u:object_r:hal_cas_default_exec:s0
/(vendor|system/vendor)/bin/hw/android\.hardware\.configstore@1\.0-service                    u:object_r:hal_configstore_default_exec:s0
# Widevine gets hal_drm_default_exec, not a widevine-specific type: Android 10's
# system/sepolicy/vendor/file_contexts labels both drm@1.0-service and
# -service-lazy as hal_drm_default_exec and declares no hal_drm_widevine_exec.
/(vendor|system/vendor)/bin/hw/android\.hardware\.drm@1\.0-service\.widevine                  u:object_r:hal_drm_default_exec:s0
/(vendor|system/vendor)/bin/hw/android\.hardware\.graphics\.composer@2\.1-service              u:object_r:hal_graphics_composer_default_exec:s0
/(vendor|system/vendor)/bin/hw/android\.hardware\.light@2\.0-service-mediatek                 u:object_r:hal_light_default_exec:s0
/(vendor|system/vendor)/bin/hw/android\.hardware\.sensors@1\.0-service-mediatek               u:object_r:hal_sensors_default_exec:s0
/(vendor|system/vendor)/bin/hw/android\.hardware\.thermal@1\.0-service                        u:object_r:hal_thermal_default_exec:s0
/(vendor|system/vendor)/bin/hw/android\.hardware\.broadcastradio@1\.1-service                 u:object_r:hal_broadcastradio_default_exec:s0

